From 75fce4be0b395f75f2db4975e1c6430ba4a845ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:35:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: only the installed core migrates a home's
 board; a SchemaAhead give-up opens a hub card

On 2026-11-12 a checkout of origin/main (95fed77843) launched against laptop-1's live ~/.hermes at 23:53:41 PST
(daveey-mini: 23:58:38) while the installed core was 2cc7101849. Its board connect added tasks.review_required,
task_events.origin_gateway and the admission_* columns to the live kanban.db; three seconds later the gateway's
own core found columns it does not declare (SchemaAhead) and gave up the Board sync role until each host's core
update, hours later. Nothing turned that into a card.

1. hermes_cli/kanban_schema_owner.py: one predicate (decide) for every board migration entry point. The home's
   installed core (<home>/hermes-agent, the checkout the launcher and hermes-core-python resolve), or a tree at
   its commit, migrates as before; a home with no install migrates as before. Any other checkout (worktree,
   scratch clone, prebuilt env at another HEAD) opening a board whose schema it would change opens it read-only
   (mode=ro): reads work, writes raise BoardSchemaNotOwned with one line naming the installed core and its
   commit, the missing columns, and `HERMES_HOME=$(mktemp -d)` for a scratch home. A board already at this
   core's schema opens normally. kanban_db_connect.connect (which init_db and every board open use) asks it
   before SCHEMA_SQL / the column pass.
2. post_update: a kanban_board_schema home step. Boot home maintenance from a non-installed checkout logs
   "skipping board migrations" and records the skip; the installed core leaves it to its first board connect.
3. hermes_cli/kanban_sync_schema_alert.py: when run_forever gives the sync role up over SchemaAhead (at start or
   mid-run), file one hub card per host incident (key kanban-sync-schema-ahead:<host>:<since>) through the
   hermes-hub courier, since this host's Board sync is down. While that host's card is open, a new incident
   comments on it instead. The card names the columns, the installed core and the newest core agent.log saw
   launching against the home. A give-up during the host's own core update (installed HEAD moved past the
   one this gateway loaded) files nothing. No Inbox.

hermes-core-wt land/ship write to the board through the installed `hermes` CLI (shutil.which("hermes")), not
the worktree's core, so they need no change.

Tests: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_schema_owner.py (a) non-installed checkout leaves PRAGMA table_info
unchanged and refuses writes with the line, (b) installed core / same-commit tree / no-install home migrate,
(c) boot home maintenance from a non-installed checkout skips board migration, (d) one hub card per incident,
a comment while open, a new card after it closes, and run_forever's give-up files it. Red on main, green here;
one mutant per case killed.

Card: t_01a1d3fb5bab541f
